# Per-host WaitingStrategy duration overrides (OPTIONAL).
#
# Copy to config/waiting_strategy.yml in the project where the runner runs to
# change the wait durations WITHOUT editing source code. The file is gitignored —
# each host keeps its own copy and edits are never committed.
#
# Two keys are honored (both in MINUTES, positive integers only):
#
#   short_wait_minutes — wait between retries in today_auto_squash mode
#                        (no task picked up before the end of workday). Default: 30.
#   long_wait_minutes  — wait between retries in daily mode (no task picked up
#                        during a daily run). Default: 60.
#
# Why per-host? The runner runs unattended on multiple machines (mini, workhorse).
# Hosts that benefit from a tight feedback loop (e.g. daily quota + frequent runs)
# can shorten both waits; hosts that should stay quiet (laptop overnight) can leave
# defaults. The fallback values match the original hard-coded durations, so a
# missing file is a safe no-op.
#
# Examples:
#   short_wait_minutes: 5
#   long_wait_minutes: 15
#
# Or pin to very long overnight intervals on a quiet host:
#   short_wait_minutes: 60
#   long_wait_minutes: 180
short_wait_minutes: 5
long_wait_minutes: 30